045417] [17592186262838 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1298261d-fd1d-57fd-8c0d-689d1739fab9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186262838 #edb/ref 1074 "We need a vector $v=⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩=\\sqrt{2}$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨3,2,-1⟩.$ So, $v⊥n$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}-{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{3} & =3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\nv=⟨{t}_{1},\\,{t}_{2},\\,3{t}_{1}+2{t}_{2}⟩,\n$$\n\nwhere ${t}_{1},{t}_{2}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{2}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{2}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,1,\\,2⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=\\frac{1}{2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263097 #edb/ref 1080 "21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263097 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263097 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a0f29de-25aa-5107-8046-0dd732f9beb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263118 #edb/ref 1080 "-90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263118 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263118 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0c504d34-49a8-5293-9654-9bb371251af7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263209 #edb/ref 1080 "18" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263209 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263209 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "162deb0b-2730-571d-b037-7db47a3aea46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263259 #edb/ref 1080 "-21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263259 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263259 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1b8f75e2-26ce-5967-ac8a-f06080423598" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263742 #edb/ref 1080 "10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186263742 #edb/ref 